Z||000001||Will||07-24-2001||08:46 AM||||Just like an SBC, the length is going to be the issue. I don't know about FoMoCo bolt patterns, but you might be able to use an SHO Taurus manual transaxle without an adapter plate, but then you'd have to get custom axles and transmission mount brackets.<P>If you elect to use the Getrag, the issues ought to be basically the same as an SBC swap.<P>Waitaminnit... doesn't the 5.0 have a front sump oil pan? That might run afoul of the exhaust, depending on how you worked the exhaust.||||reg||1
Z||000002||gtcash||07-24-2001||09:34 AM||||"FAGETABADIT"||||reg||6
Z||000003||Patrick's Dad||07-24-2001||10:10 AM||||Two things:<P>First, if what you really want is a 4.9 Fiero, then this is the motor. Ford's marketing guys came up with the 5.0 thing, but the 302ci engine is 4875 cc's, or, rounded up, is 4.9l. BTW, the 302 is only rated at 225hp. Why not get an LS1 (5.7l) at 300+ hp? If you want a real 5.0, use a Chevy 305.<P>Second, based on my recent Ford Explorer experience, it will leak oil, and, if you use a FoMoCo transmission, tranny fluid, and will be harder to work on than your Fiero is currently. I never worried about the Firestone tires, but when the driver's door wouldn't close into the frame (dropped over 3/4"), that was it. Ford sucks so much that I've heard that Hoover, Eureka, and Oreck are trying to hire away their R&D guys.<P>||||reg||13
Z||000004||Archie||07-24-2001||02:31 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Will:<BR><B>Just like an SBC, the length is going to be the issue. I<BR>Waitaminnit... doesn't the 5.0 have a front sump oil pan? That might run afoul of the exhaust, depending on how you worked the exhaust.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Also you'll find that the FMC distributor ends up right beneath the right side hinge rib on the underside of the decklid. With a distributor cap on it, it'll hit big time.<P>Archie<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||rockcrawl||07-24-2001||04:00 PM||||I think the SBF is shorter and lighter than the SBC, but I still think it's a waste of time. Too much BS to overcome like the distributor location as Archie mentioned. If you've got lots of time and money to spend, it sounds like an exciting project, but not one I'd ever want to take on.<P>Hey Patric's Dad, <BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Ford sucks so much that I've heard that Hoover, Eureka, and Oreck are trying to hire away their R&D guys.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I'm sorry you feel that way, it sounds like you had a bad experience. But just remember, the best selling truck in the US has been a Ford for over 20 years running. There's a reason they are #1.||||reg||1
